  anyway. [3mComplexity: moderate.[0m

  [1mB. Identity module, global namespace[0m
  Same module contents, but [38;5;153midentity.js[39m loads via a second plain [38;5;153m<script>[39m tag and attaches [38;5;153mwindow.AppIdentity[39m. Buys zero
  tooling change — [38;5;153mfile://[39m keeps working, load order in [38;5;153mindex.html[39m is the only new rule. Costs: a global, an implicit
  script-order dependency that breaks silently if someone reorders the tags, and awkward testing. [3mComplexity: trivial.[0m

  [1mC. Event bus over [38;5;153msessionStorage[0m
  No shared import: login writes the key and dispatches an [38;5;153midentity:changed[39m event; consumers subscribe. Buys decoupling
  and cross-tab sync for free via the native [38;5;153mstorage[39m event. Costs: consumers still have to agree on the storage key by
  convention, so you get the coupling without a module to enforce it — indirection that pays off at a scale this app is
  nowhere near. [3mComplexity: moderate.[0m I'd discard this one unless cross-tab sync is a stated requirement.

  [1mRecommendation: A.[0m The whole point of your answer to question 2 was that other forms will need this later; A is the
  option where "later" means one import line rather than a convention everyone has to remember. B is the fallback if
  double-click-to-open matters to your workflow.

  [1mOne thing all three force, which I want on the record:[0m a server-issued ID arrives over the network, so [38;5;153mlogin()[39m has to
  become asynchronous — [38;5;153masync function login(...)[39m returning a Promise, with the caller awaiting it. It's stubbed and
  synchronous today ([38;5;153mapp.js:4-8[39m), so nothing breaks right now, but this is a second change to [38;5;153mlogin()[39m's contract on top
  of it not gaining the [38;5;153muserId[39m parameter you originally asked for. Doing it now avoids re-breaking every caller when the
  real POST lands.

